    {
      "id": "notre_dame",
      "title": "Notre-Dame de Paris",
      "text": "Notre-Dame stands on an island in the river Seine. People began to build it more than 850 years ago. In 2019 a fire burned its roof. It was mended, and it opened again in December 2024."
    },
    {
      "id": "asking",
      "title": "Asking the way",
      "text": "To find your way on foot in Paris, you ask. People answer in streets and turns: la première rue à droite, tout droit, traversez le pont."
    },
    {
      "id": "church",
      "title": "Inside a church",
      "text": "The altar is the big table at the front of a church. Inside, people keep their voices low, even visitors."
    }
  ],
